[17.305849, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Smb Eternalblue campaign\r\n=======================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: smb-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.218\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\n"]
[17.305982, "o", "finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1210\r\nExploitation of Remote Services\r\n[lateral-movement] step 1: SMBv1\r\nexploitation (CVE-2017-0144)\r\nT1059.001 PowerShell\r\n[execution] step 2: PowerShell\r\nexecution\r\nT1003.001 LSASS Memory\r\n[credential-access] step 3: LSASS\r\ncredential dump\r\nT1486\r\nData Encrypted for Impact\r\n[impact] step 4: ransomware\r\nencryption\r\nT1546.003 Windows Management Instrumentation Event Subscription [privilege-escalation]\r\nstep 5: WMI event subscription\r\nT1574.001 DLL\r\n[stealth] step 6: DLL search-order\r\nhijack\r\nT1070.001 Clear Windows Event Logs\r\n[defense-evasion] step 7: System\r\nevent log clear\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\nCVE-2017-0144 CVSS 8.8 (HIGH) v3.1 CWE=The SMBv1 server in Microsoft Windows Vista SP2; Windows Server 2008 SP2 and R2 SP1;\r\nWindows 7 SP1; Windows 8.1; Windows Server 2012 Gold and R2; Windows RT 8.1; and Windows 10\r\nGold, 1511, and 1607; and Windows Server 2016 allows remote att\r\nref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/154690/DOUBLEPULSAR-Payload-Execution-Neutraliz\r\nation.html\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.218\r\nc2 update-smb[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]smb[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n"]
