[139.12597, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[139.12641, "o", "# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-1677  (DRAFT — reconcile against your findings)"]
[139.126505, "o", "\r\n"]
[139.12664, "o", "\r\n> A previous shift pre-filled this remediation ticket from the SAS alerts ALONE. It is known\r\n> to be incomplete and contains stale/incorrect lines. Correct it IN PLACE against your own\r\n> investigation of /disk; cite evidence for every change. Do not author from scratch.\r\n\r\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 203.0.113.9 | proposed | STALE: prior shift used the wrong IP; confirm the real origin from /disk |\r\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) | RDP | proposed | WRONG: not the entry vector for this host — verify against /sas/cti |\r\n"]
[139.126753, "o", "| 3 | Remove cron miner | /var/spool/cron/root | DONE | UNVERIFIED: marked done with no evidence — re-check |\r\n| 4 | (add) silent persistence you discover | /Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA | TODO | ticket omits everything not alerted — add the rest |\r\n\r\n"]
[139.126784, "o", "## Reviewer checklist\r\n- [ ] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\r\n- [ ] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\r\n- [ ] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\r\n- [ ] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\r\n"]
[139.126972, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@688114a882eb:/app# "]
[154.262127, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\n# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-1677  (RECONCILED)\n\n> Reconciled change ticket updated following forensic investigation of `/disk` and cross-referencing `/sas` telemetry and CTI advisories.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.218 | proposed | Corrected origin IP from 203.0.113.9 to 198.51.100.218 based on C2 beacon in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` and `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 EternalBlue / Disable SMBv1) | /Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys | proposed | Corrected CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep RDP) to CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue SMBv1). Host compromised via SMBv1. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\n| 3 | Remove cron miner / Audit miner tasks | /var/spool/cron/root | REJECTED | Downgraded from DONE: Target path /var/spool/cron/root is invalid for Windows target host `smb-prod-01`. Miner XMRig pool strings are embedded in Windows binaries (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`). |\n| 4 | Remove WMI event subscription persistence | /Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA | proposed | Added silent persistence: Attacker created `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer` in WMI repository. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\n| 5 | Quarantine hijacked DLL | /Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll | proposed | Added silent stealth finding: DLL search-order hijack / sideload binary `wbemcomn.dll` placed in wbem folder. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 6 | Audit log clearing and restore logs | /Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx | proposed | Added silent defense evasion: Attacker cleared event log (EventID 1102). Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n| 7 | Quarantine exploit implant binary | /Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe | proposed | Added exploit implant containment: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 8 | Quarantine LSASS dump & perform credential reset | /Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp | proposed | Added credential access mitigation: LSASS dump file dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`. Force password resets. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 9 | Quarantine ransomware payload & isolate host | /Users/Public/enc.exe | proposed | Added impact mitigation: Ransomware binary dropped at `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`. Evidence: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under `/disk` or `/sas`\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to REJECTED/OPEN with evidence\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\nEOF\n"]
[154.26291, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.264572, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> # CHANGE TICKET  CHG-1677  (RECONCILED)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> > Reconciled change ticket updated following forensic investigation of `/disk` and cross-referencing `/sas` telemetry and CTI advisories.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|------|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.218 | proposed | Corrected origin IP from 203.0.113.9 to 198.51.100.218 based on C2 beacon in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` and `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 EternalBlue / Disable SMBv1) | /Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys | proposed | Corrected CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep RDP) to CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue SMBv1). Host compromised via SMBv1. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 3 | Remove cron miner / Audit miner tasks | /var/spool/cron/root | REJECTED | Downgraded from DONE: Target path /var/spool/cron/root is invalid for Windows target host `smb-prod-01`. Miner XMRig pool strings are embedded in Windows binaries (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`). |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.264807, "o", "| 4 | Remove WMI event subscription persistence | /Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA | proposed | Added silent persistence: Attacker created `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer` in WMI repository. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.264918, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.265213, "o", "| 5 | Quarantine hijacked DLL | /Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll | proposed | Added silent stealth finding: DLL search-order hijack / sideload binary `wbemcomn.dll` placed in wbem folder. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.265645, "o", "| 6 | Audit log clearing and restore logs | /Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx | proposed | Added silent defense evasion: Attacker cleared event log (EventID 1102). Evidence: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.265787, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.266097, "o", "| 7 | Quarantine exploit implant binary | /Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe | proposed | Added exploit implant containment: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.26645, "o", "| 8 | Quarantine LSASS dump & perform credential reset | /Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp | proposed | Added credential access mitigation: LSASS dump file dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`. Force password resets. Evidence: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[154.266757, "o", "| 9 | Quarantine ransomware payload & isolate host | /Users/Public/enc.exe | proposed | Added impact mitigation: Ransomware binary dropped at `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`. Evidence: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[154.266823, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[154.266871, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
