[220.619911, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n**Host:** `smb-prod-01`  \n**Ticket Reference:** Change Ticket CHG-1677 (Reconciled)  \n**Strategy Principle:** Prefer backup, isolation, and quarantine over immediate destructive deletion.  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1677)\n\n| # | Action Item | Target Path / System | Status | Forensic Justification & Evidence Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound at firewall | `198.51.100.218` | Proposed | Corrected source IP from `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.218`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 / Disable SMBv1 | `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` | Proposed | Corrected CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) to CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue SMBv1). Entry vector driver. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json` |\n| 3 | Reject Linux cron miner row / Audit scheduled tasks | `/var/spool/cron/root` | REJECTED | Target path is non-existent on Windows host `smb-prod-01`. Miner XMRig pool strings were found embedded in Windows DLL `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 4 | Quarantine WMI event subscription persistence | `/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Attacker created `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer`. Backup repository before rebuilding WMI namespace. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\n| 5 | Quarantine hijacked DLL | `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Sideloaded malicious DLL in `wbem` directory. Backup and move to isolated quarantine directory. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 6 | Restore System Event Log & configure SIEM forwarding | `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Anti-forensics Event ID 1102 log clearing observed. Backup cleared log for offsite forensics and restore baseline logging. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n| 7 | Quarantine exploit implant | `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` | Proposed | Added containment item: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped in Temp folder. Backup and move to quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 8 | Quarantine LSASS dump & perform domain credential resets | `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` | Proposed | Added credential recovery item: LSASS dump file captured by attacker. Quarantine file and force password resets for all active accounts on host. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 9 | Quarantine ransomware payload & isolate host | `/Users/Public/enc.exe` | Proposed | Added impact containment item: Ransomware binary dropped in Public directory. Isolate network interface and backup/quarantine binary. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Phase-by-Phase Execution Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation\n1. **Network Containment:** Isolate host `smb-prod-01` from internal VLANs while retaining out-of-band management connectivity.\n2. **Firewall Rule Update:** Block inbound and outbound traffic to/from C2 IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\n3. **SMB Service Containment:** Stop the Server service (`net stop lanmanserver`) to immediately stop further SMBv1 exploitation.\n\n### Phase 2: Preservative Quarantine & Eradication\n1. **File Quarantine (Not Direct Deletion):** Create encrypted quarantine directory (`C:\\Quarantine\\SOC-2026-0811\\`) and move malicious binaries/dumps:\n   - Move `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.\n   - Move `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.\n   - Move `/Users/Public/enc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.\n   - Move `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/"]
[220.619936, "i", "Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n2. **WMI Persistence Removal:** Backup WMI repository (`/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to quarantine, then execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription | Remove-CimInstance` to purge unauthorized `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` instances. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\n3. **Vulnerability Eradication:** Disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart`) and apply security update MS17-010 / KB4012212 to update `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\n4. **Credential Revocation:** Perform mandatory password reset for local Administrator, Domain accounts, and service accounts logged onto `smb-prod-01`. Revoke cached Kerberos tickets / NTLM hashes. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\n\n### Phase 3: Recovery & Verification\n1. **System Restoration:** Reboot system into safe mode, verify `srv.sys` is updated, ensure `wbemcomn.dll` in `wbem` directory is removed, and confirm no rogue WMI consumers exist.\n2. **SIEM & Logging Verification:** Verify central logging via Winlogbeat/Syslog is capturing active events from `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.\n3. **Network Verification:** Run vulnerability scan against host `smb-prod-01` on port 445/tcp to confirm SMBv1 is disabled and MS17-010 is resolved. Citation: `/sas/vulns.json`.\n4. **Re-integration:** Re-connect network interface to production network under monitoring for 72 hours.\nEOF\n"]
