[220.624174, "o", "## 2. Phase-by-Phase Execution Plan\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.624235, "o", "### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[220.62427, "o", "> "]
[220.62441, "o", "1. **Network Containment:** Isolate host `smb-prod-01` from internal VLANs while retaining out-of-band management connectivity.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[220.624432, "o", "> "]
[220.624643, "o", "2. **Firewall Rule Update:** Block inbound and outbound traffic to/from C2 IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.624784, "o", "3. **SMB Service Containment:** Stop the Server service (`net stop lanmanserver`) to immediately stop further SMBv1 exploitation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[220.62482, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.625768, "o", "### Phase 2: Preservative Quarantine & Eradication\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 1. **File Quarantine (Not Direct Deletion):** Create encrypted quarantine directory (`C:\\Quarantine\\SOC-2026-0811\\`) and move malicious binaries/dumps:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Move `/Users/Public/enc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 2. **WMI Persistence Removal:** Backup WMI repository (`/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to quarantine, then execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription | Remove-CimInstance` to purge unauthorized `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` instances. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.625965, "o", "3. **Vulnerability Eradication:** Disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart`) and apply security update MS17-010 / KB4012212 to update `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.6262, "o", "4. **Credential Revocation:** Perform mandatory password reset for local Administrator, Domain accounts, and service accounts logged onto `smb-prod-01`. Revoke cached Kerberos tickets / NTLM hashes. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[220.626228, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[220.62626, "o", "> "]
[220.626315, "o", "### Phase 3: Recovery & Verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[220.626326, "o", "> "]
[220.62653, "o", "1. **System Restoration:** Reboot system into safe mode, verify `srv.sys` is updated, ensure `wbemcomn.dll` in `wbem` directory is removed, and confirm no rogue WMI consumers exist.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[220.626546, "o", "> "]
[220.62684, "o", "2. **SIEM & Logging Verification:** Verify central logging via Winlogbeat/Syslog is capturing active events from `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.626973, "o", "3. **Network Verification:** Run vulnerability scan against host `smb-prod-01` on port 445/tcp to confirm SMBv1 is disabled and MS17-010 is resolved. Citation: `/sas/vulns.json`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[220.627122, "o", "4. **Re-integration:** Re-connect network interface to production network under monitoring for 72 hours.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
